"{\"search\":{\"query\":\"\",\"type\":\"Contract\",\"categories\":[\"InformationTechnology\"],\"geo\":[{\"latLong\":[0],\"location\":\"\",\"distance\":null}],\"states\":[],\"countries\":[\"USA\"],\"remoteOnly\":false},\"searchTimestamp\":1792554435671,\"hits\":[{\"jobOrderId\":1157593,\"title\":\"Content Operations Consultant\",\"description\":\"Our client is currently seeking a Content Operations Consultant \\t\\t\\t<br><p class=\\\"paragraph\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><b>Description: </b></p><p class=\\\"paragraph\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><b>You will be responsible for:</b></p><p class=\\\"paragraph\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"\\\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>DAM process design: </b>Define and document end-to-end processes for content intake, review, approval, publishing, reuse, archival and retirement.</p><p class=\\\"paragraph\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"\\\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Content operations: </b>Coordinate day-to-day DAM activities and ensure assets, components, source files and related content are managed according to established procedures.</p><p class=\\\"paragraph\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"\\\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Metadata management: </b>Maintain metadata quality through validation, enrichment, standardization and remediation to support accurate content classification.</p><p class=\\\"paragraph\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"\\\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Taxonomy and tagging: </b>Apply and maintain taxonomy, tagging standards and controlled vocabularies to improve content organization, search and discoverability.</p><p class=\\\"paragraph\\\" dir=\\\"ltr\\\" style=\\\"\\\">·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Content quality and compliance: </b>Perform quality checks to ensure content and metadata meet defined operational, governance and lifecycle requirements.</p>\",\"location\":\"REMOTE\",\"salary\":\" $45.00 USD Hourly - $50.00 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1792053410000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"},{\"jobOrderId\":1155523,\"title\":\"Full Stack Java Developer\",\"description\":\"<h3 style=\\\"\\\">Onsite 1 Day per month in Worcester, MA</h3><h3 style=\\\"\\\">Overview</h3><p>A dynamic team is seeking a skilled Full Stack Java Developer to contribute to the development of a cutting-edge digital platform supporting R&amp;D initiatives in biotherapeutics. This contract role involves hands-on software development across both frontend and backend systems, delivering enterprise-scale informatics solutions for entity management in early-stage therapeutic research.</p><h3 style=\\\"\\\">Key Responsibilities</h3><ul><li><p>Develop high-quality, maintainable, and well-documented software solutions following industry best practices</p></li><li><p>Participate in code reviews, architectural discussions, and documentation efforts</p></li><li><p>Collaborate with cross-functional teams to gather requirements, develop features, test functionality, and support deployment and training</p></li><li><p>Adhere to established project management methodologies, documentation protocols, and continuous improvement practices</p></li></ul><h3 style=\\\"\\\">Required Skills &amp; Experience</h3><ul><li><p>Strong backend development experience using the Java ecosystem</p></li><li><p>Proficiency in frontend development with AngularJS, JavaScript, TypeScript, or React</p></li><li><p>Solid understanding of software engineering principles, system design, and lifecycle management</p></li><li><p>Experience building RESTful APIs and implementing ETL processes</p></li><li><p>\",\"location\":\"Worcester, MA\",\"salary\":\" $40.00 USD Hourly - $65.00 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1790939736000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"},{\"jobOrderId\":1155313,\"title\":\"Data Retrieval Specialist\",\"description\":\"<div style=\\\"\\\"><p><strong>Data Retrieval Specialist</strong><br><strong>Location:</strong> Remote/Telecommute (California)<br><strong>Travel Requirement:</strong> Frequent travel to provider offices throughout San Bernardino and Riverside Counties<br><strong>Assignment Type:</strong> Short-Term Contract<br><strong>Pay Rate:</strong> $33.02/hr</p><h3>Position Overview</h3><p>Seeking a detail-oriented <strong>Data Retrieval Specialist</strong> to support quality initiatives including <strong>HEDIS, Risk Adjustment, quality reporting, and special healthcare projects</strong>. This short-term assignment is ideal for candidates with healthcare data collection experience and proficiency navigating Electronic Medical Record (EMR) systems.</p><p>Under the direction of the Data Quality team, this role is responsible for collecting, tracking, researching, validating, and managing medical record data from provider offices while ensuring compliance with regulatory and quality reporting requirements. The position requires strong organizational skills, communication abilities, and the capacity to manage multiple projects and deadlines in a fast-paced environment.</p><h3>Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>Coordinate and manage scheduling, retrieval, tracking, monitoring, and quality assurance of medical record collection activities.</li><li>Collect and validate data supporting HEDIS, Risk Adjustment, Quality, and regulatory reporting initiatives.</li><li>\",\"location\":\"Rancho Cucamonga, CA\",\"salary\":\" $30.00 USD Hourly - $33.02 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1790856211000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"},{\"jobOrderId\":1158217,\"title\":\"Sr Automation Engineer\",\"description\":\"<ul style=\\\"\\\" type=\\\"disc\\\"><li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Job      Title:</b> IT Senior Automation Engineer<o:p></o:p></li>  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Location:</b>      Remote (Must be available during EST business hours)<o:p></o:p></li>  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Employment      Type:</b> Contract<o:p></o:p></li>  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Duration:</b>      Initial 6-month engagement with strong extension potential<o:p></o:p></li> </ul>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>&nbsp;</b>Our client is seeking a highly skilled <b>Senior Automation Engineer</b> to join Automation &amp; Productivity team. This role is ideal for someone who thrives at the intersection of <b>Robotic Process Automation (RPA), Artificial Intelligence, and modern software engineering</b>.</p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p>You will lead the design, development, and delivery of intelligent automation solutions that drive operational efficiency, reduce manual effort, and enhance business productivity. Beyond building automation, you'll play a critical role in evaluating where AI, RPA, or a hybrid approach can deliver the greatest business value.</p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\">This is a hands-on technical leadership role requiring expertise in <b>UiPath, React, API integrations, AI/LLM technologies, and production automation support</b>.<o:p></o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Key Responsibilities</b></p>  <ul style=\\\"\\\" type=\\\"disc\\\">  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\">\",\"location\":\"REMOTE\",\"salary\":\" $80.00 USD Hourly - $85.00 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1792500029000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"},{\"jobOrderId\":1158196,\"title\":\"Network Project Manager - II\",\"description\":\"Our client is currently seeking a Fixed Wireless Access Network Project Manager.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br><br>Role is 100% remote.<div><br> \\t\\t\\t<b>This job will have the following responsibilities:</b><ul> \\t\\t\\t</ul> \\t\\t\\t<div><p style=\\\"\\\">Responsibilities:</p><br style=\\\"\\\"><ul style=\\\"\\\"> <li style=\\\"\\\">Managing a diversity of MDU/MTU build projects across different marktes in parallel.</li> <li style=\\\"\\\">Analyzes MDU/MTU addressing, architecture and site survey designs.</li> <li style=\\\"\\\">Scheduling and tracking build start dates with property owners</li> <li style=\\\"\\\">Interface with field engineering, general contractors, and sales organizations to serve and support proper MDU/MTU build designs.</li> <li style=\\\"\\\">Track progress to ensure Open For Sales (OFS) targets are met.</li> </ul><span style=\\\"\\\"> </span><p style=\\\"\\\">Must Have Skills:</p><span style=\\\"\\\"> </span><ul style=\\\"\\\"> <li style=\\\"\\\">Proven track record of managing high-volume pipelines of projects.</li> <li style=\\\"\\\">Deep understanding of 5G/Fixed Wireless Access (FWA) architecture, specifically MDU builds and donor site dynamics.</li> <li style=\\\"\\\">Experience with address validation, property/parcel ID (PID) management, and GIS-based tools.</li> </ul><span style=\\\"\\\"> </span><p style=\\\"\\\">Desired Skills:</p><span style=\\\"\\\"> </span><ul style=\\\"\\\"> <li style=\\\"\\\">Precision: Obsessive attention to detail—ensuring MDU/MTU build packages are \\\"whole and correct\\\" the first time.</li> <li style=\\\"\\\">\",\"location\":\"Dallas, TX\",\"salary\":\" $50.00 USD Hourly - $55.00 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1792494403000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"},{\"jobOrderId\":1158159,\"title\":\"AI Security Engineer\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Position Title:</b> Information Security Engineer – AI-Driven Coding<br> <b>Experience Level:</b> Senior<br> <b>Target Start Date:</b> 11/30/2026<br> <b>Duration:</b> 6 month contract<br> <b>Work Location:</b> Pontiac, MI - Hybrid (2 days a week on site)<br> <!--[if !supportLineBreakNewLine]--><br> <!--[endif]--><o:p></o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Position Overview</b><o:p></o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\">We are seeking a senior Information Security Engineer to implement and configure security controls for AI-driven coding tools within its development environment. The contractor will secure AI coding agents, establish appropriate access and execution restrictions, integrate security configurations with Docker and Azure DevOps, validate controls, document gaps, and transition the solution to staff.<o:p></o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\">This is a hands-on security engineering role focused on securing AI-assisted software development, not AI/ML model development.<o:p></o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>&nbsp;</b></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Key Responsibilities</b><o:p></o:p></p>  <ul style=\\\"\\\" type=\\\"disc\\\">  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\">Configure      security controls for AI-driven coding tools, including permissions,      execution restrictions, network access controls, credential protection,      and logging.<o:p></o:p></li>  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\">\",\"location\":\"Pontiac, MI\",\"salary\":\" $60.00 USD Hourly - $65.00 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1792486880000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"},{\"jobOrderId\":1158116,\"title\":\"Senior Project Manager\",\"description\":\"<p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b><span style=\\\"\\\">Senior Project Manager<o:p></o:p></span></b></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><span style=\\\"\\\">Long Term contract - Hybrid (2 days per week on site)<br> <b>Experience Level:</b> Senior<br> <b>Target Start Date:</b> November 16, 2026<br> <b>Duration:</b> Ongoing Contract<o:p></o:p></span></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b><span style=\\\"\\\">&nbsp;</span></b></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b><span style=\\\"\\\">Position Overview</span></b><span style=\\\"\\\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><span style=\\\"\\\">We are seeking a Senior Project Manager to support its Information Security division. This individual will oversee one or more projects, coordinate project teams and resources, maintain schedules and budgets, and monitor project progress through completion. The Project Manager will serve as a liaison between project team members and the functional areas requesting project support.<o:p></o:p></span></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b><span style=\\\"\\\">&nbsp;</span></b></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b><span style=\\\"\\\">Key Responsibilities</span></b><span style=\\\"\\\"><o:p></o:p></span></p>  <ul type=\\\"disc\\\">  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><span style=\\\"\\\">Oversee one or more projects from planning through      execution.<o:p></o:p></span></li>  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><span style=\\\"\\\">Assemble project teams and assign individual      responsibilities.<o:p></o:p></span></li>  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\" style=\\\"\\\"><span style=\\\"\\\">\",\"location\":\"Pontiac, MI\",\"salary\":\" $55.00 USD Hourly - $65.00 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1792485844000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"},{\"jobOrderId\":1158078,\"title\":\"UX Engineer (III)\",\"description\":\"Our client is currently seeking a UX Engineer (III) \\t\\t\\t<br><br><ul> \\t\\t\\t</ul> \\t\\t\\t<div><p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Project Overview<o:p></o:p></b></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\">This role offers a unique blend of rapid prototyping, design exploration, and technical execution. You will play a pivotal role in transforming abstract concepts into interactive prototypes that explore future user-facing products, as well as developing AI-powered tools that enhance internal workflows. Your work will enable teams to learn directly from users, inspire product vision with what is possible, and establish a tangible path forward for integrating cutting-edge AI technologies into core experiences.<o:p></o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Minimum Qualifications<o:p></o:p></b></p>  <ul style=\\\"\\\" type=\\\"disc\\\">  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>5+      years of experience</b> in front-end development, technical UX design, or      interactive prototyping.<o:p></o:p></li> </ul>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p>  <p class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Your Mindset &amp; Approach<o:p></o:p></b></p>  <ul style=\\\"\\\" type=\\\"disc\\\">  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Thrive      in Ambiguity:</b> You are energized by environments where the problem      space is undefined, technology is evolving, and the path forward is      open-ended. You excel at creating structure, clarity, and direction in      uncharted territory.<o:p></o:p></li>  <li class=\\\"MsoNormal\\\"><b>Think      by Making:</b>\",\"location\":\"San Bruno, CA\",\"salary\":\" $95.00 USD Hourly - $115.00 USD Hourly\",\"opened\":1792428332000,\"score\":0,\"category\":{\"categoryId\":7,\"description\":\"Information Technology\"},\"type\":\"Contract\"}],\"total\":466,\"scrollId\":null,\"size\":20,\"offset\":0}"